# Lexicon: copy to .env and fill in. Do not commit .env.

# --- Primary user ---
# Required for Self-evaluation and retrospectives: meeting notes include "What I did well / could improve."
# Without this, the system doesn't know who "I" is. Init syncs it to Metadata/User.md.
LEXICON_USER_NAME=

# --- Fireflies (per account) ---
# Default account is "personal". Use company name or another label for a second account (e.g. "acme").
# Area = Lexicon context for notes/memory (e.g. personal, company, career, general). If account name is not the area (e.g. "acme"), set AREA_acme=company so notes go to Meetings/company/.

# Account: personal (default)
FIREFLIES_API_KEY_personal=
EMAIL_personal=
AREA_personal=personal

# Account: company (or acme, etc.)
# FIREFLIES_API_KEY_acme=
# EMAIL_acme=
# AREA_acme=company

# --- Areas ---
# Areas: personal, company, career, friendship, general (Meetings/<Area>/, People/<Area>/, Memory/<Area>/).
# Full list and descriptions: Metadata/area_registry.md
# Fireflies: AREA_<account> sets the *default* area written into transcript frontmatter.
# (PROJECT_<account> still works -- kept for existing .env files.)
# The summarize step may override it if the meeting content belongs to a different area.
# Manual: set area in transcript frontmatter only (folder is Transcripts/Manual/, not area-based).

# --- HiDock (hinotes_organizer) ---
# See docs/SETUP.md § HiDock. Clone hinotes_organizer; set its config output.dir to:
#   <this-vault>/Transcripts/HiDock
HIDOCK_ORGANIZER_ROOT=
# HIDOCK_CONFIG=/path/to/hinotes_organizer/config.yaml
